/**
\fn pdg::Port* pdg::GraphicsManager::createOffscreenPort(const Rect& rect)
\brief Create a persistent transparent RGBA drawing surface without a window.

\param rect Supplies positive integer pixel dimensions within the backend's texture
limit. Its origin is ignored; Port coordinates start at (0, 0).
\return A manager-owned Port, or nullptr for invalid dimensions or graphics allocation
failure. Close it with closeGraphicsPort(); do not delete it directly or use it afterward.

Use ordinary Port drawing methods, Attributes, fonts, Drawings, and clipping. The surface
starts transparent and retains drawing. It receives no automatic PortDraw events and is
not cleared by the frame loop. It never becomes the main port.

\note Available in graphics-enabled builds. No existing main port or visible window is
required. A port created with an existing main window shares its context and is closed
when that window closes. Images already created from it remain valid.
\note API stability: 2 — Evolving.
\see Image::createImageFromOffscreenPort(), closeGraphicsPort()
*/

/**
\fn pdg::Image* pdg::Image::createImageFromOffscreenPort(Port* port, bool copyPixels)
\brief Create a snapshot or a live image of an offscreen surface.

\param port An open offscreen Port.
\param copyPixels Defaults to true for an independent copy. False retains the shared
surface and reflects subsequent drawing without copying its pixels for rendering within
the same graphics context.
\return An Image owning one reference, or nullptr for null or onscreen ports. Call release()
when finished. The image has the port's pixel dimensions and transparency.

Both modes survive closure of the source port. A live image keeps its surface alive after
the Port is closed; drawing through the closed Port is invalid. Destruction of the underlying
graphics context preserves the surface's final pixels for surviving images. Pixel reads
and serialization read the current contents; deserialization produces an independent
snapshot. Rendering across independent graphics contexts or into the source surface uses
a snapshot. setTransparentColor() detaches a live image before changing its pixels.

\note Available in graphics-enabled builds. The current Port clip does not crop the
result. Image opacity is independent of the shared surface.
\note API stability: 2 — Evolving.

\par Example
\code{.cpp}
auto& graphics = pdg::GraphicsManager::instance();
auto* surface = graphics.createOffscreenPort(pdg::Rect(128, 128));
if (surface) {
    auto* live = pdg::Image::createImageFromOffscreenPort(surface, false);
    surface->drawRect(pdg::Rect(16, 16, 112, 112),
        pdg::Attributes().fillColor(pdg::Color(1.0f, 0.0f, 0.0f))
            .lineStyle(pdg::lineStyle_None));
    // live now displays the red rectangle; later surface drawing updates it.
    graphics.closeGraphicsPort(surface);
    if (live) live->release();
}
\endcode
\see GraphicsManager::createOffscreenPort(), Port::drawImage(), getPixel()
*/

/**
\fn pdg::Port& pdg::Port::clear(const Color& color)
\brief Replace pixels inside the current clip with an exact color.
\param color Defaults to transparent black. Alpha replaces the previous alpha;
this differs from drawing a translucent rectangle, which blends with existing pixels.

Works on graphics-enabled onscreen and offscreen ports. The current clip is unchanged.
Live images made from an offscreen port reflect the clear on their next draw.
\note API stability: 2 — Evolving.
\see setClipRect(), resetClipRect(), GraphicsManager::createOffscreenPort()
*/

/**
\fn pdg::Port& pdg::Port::setDrawingOrigin(const Point& origin)
\brief Set the Port coordinate at the top left of an offscreen surface.
\param origin Finite coordinates for the drawing area's top left. Initially (0, 0).

Pixel dimensions and stored pixels do not change. getDrawingArea() reports the new
origin and the clip resets to that area. Drawing and clipping now use those coordinates;
Image pixel coordinates remain zero-based. This supports rendering a View into a reusable
surface without changing its layout coordinates. Onscreen ports and nonfinite origins
are rejected with an error.
\note Requires a Port from GraphicsManager::createOffscreenPort().
\note API stability: 2 — Evolving.
\see clear(), getDrawingArea(), Image::createImageFromOffscreenPort()
*/
